title: "Birds of Kenya: a bird identification tool for Kenyan species (Birdiie)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kemboi
    given-names: Milsort
version: "2.1"
date-released: 2026-10-24
license: AGPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/KemboiM/birds-of-kenya"
url: "https://kemboim.github.io/birds-of-kenya/"
keywords:
  - bird identification
  - Kenya
  - computer vision
  - object detection
  - image classification
  - YOLO
  - MobileNetV2
  - biodiversity
abstract: >-
  A two-stage bird identification tool for Kenyan species. A YOLO detector finds every
  bird in a photo and a MobileNetV2 classifier, trained on GBIF photos of 547 Kenyan
  species, names each one. It counts birds by species, describes each species and
  estimates distance. The Birdiie web app runs the models on Android and iOS phones.
